// With `runFirst`, the killed git does its work first: the rebase stops on its
// conflict and its abort succeeds. A rebase killed before it starts leaves
// nothing to abort, so the abort fails too and only the interrupt check on
// the rebase's own error keeps the Ctrl-C from becoming a fail steered to the worker.
it.each([
  ['the rebase', isRebase, true],
  ['the rebase before it starts', isRebase, false],
  ['the abort of a conflicting rebase', isAbort, false],
